      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T21:52:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding a `sharedContext()` method to `Resource.h`, calling that, and casting it to `DawnSharedContext` every time we need access to the Dawn shared context in this class seems a but unnecessary. It seems like you only use this method to have access to the `DawnSharedContext` within `onMap` and `onUnmap`.\n\nAs an alternative, could we simply store a pointer to the `DawnSharedContext` as a private class member of `DawnBuffer` when it\u0027s passed in to `DawnBuffer::Make(...)` and reference that instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "243ccf9c2bbb7c0d1224bbc5b94a4f2e9f53330a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "493dd10b_01a50134",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 7953
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T23:45:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I though the `fSharedContext` in the `Resource` is for accessing from child classes, since `Resource` doesn\u0027t really use `fSharedContext` except setting it null while destroying.\n\nAnd I feel it is better to not duplicated this pointer in every child classes.\n1. it reduces class size.\n2. avoid duplicated code (`internalDispose()`) for setting it to null in every child class during destroying.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "227a52df_ba335e83",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "243ccf9c2bbb7c0d1224bbc5b94a4f2e9f53330a",
